    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner's tier becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the existing `namesakeCount` pattern (compute-on-create \u2192 persist \u2192 read via mapper):\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field with getter/setter (`household_size` column).\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the `householdId` is assigned, set `householdSize` to the count of existing owners sharing that `householdId` **plus one** (the owner being created \u2014 i.e. \"after this create\"). Added a `countHouseholdMembers` helper.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the existing SILVER (unique name + email present) / BRONZE logic.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `household_size` column so JPA maps cleanly under each dialect.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed uses positional inserts, so I added the corresponding trailing `NULL` to each owner row (the h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists and mysql has none, so they needed no change).\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` acceptance test passes).",
